    ↓
1. Determine action details
    ├─ Action: What was done (BanUser, WarnPost, etc)
    ├─ Entity: What was affected (User, Post, etc)
    ├─ EntityId: ID of affected entity
    ├─ OldValue: Previous value (if applicable)
    ├─ NewValue: New value (if applicable)
    ├─ Description: Human-readable description
    ↓
2. Extract request context
    ├─ Admin user ID
    ├─ Client IP address
    ├─ Timestamp
    ↓
3. Create AuditLog record
    ├─ UserId: Admin who performed action
    ├─ Action: Action type
    ├─ Entity: Entity type
    ├─ EntityId: Entity ID
    ├─ OldValue: Previous state
    ├─ NewValue: New state
    ├─ Description: Details
    ├─ IpAddress: Source IP
    ├─ CreatedAt: UTC timestamp
    ↓
4. Save to database asynchronously
    ├─ Use Task.Run() for async save
    ├─ Prevent blocking user action
    ↓
5. Log to file
    ├─ Include timestamp, action, entity
```

**Audit Specializations:**

